.TH "CARGO\-START" "1"
.nh
.ad l
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "NAME"
cargo\-start \[em] Start an experimental Ohm workspace check session
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBcargo \-Zohm\-check\-session start \-\-source\fR \fISOURCE\fR [\fIcheck\-options\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Start a workspace\-local compiler host, perform the first check, and return. Later
\fBcargo\-check\fR(1) commands in the same workspace can reuse its warm compiler
state. \fBcargo\-stop\fR(1) shuts down the host and its compiler. A failed first
check leaves the session available for repairs.
.sp
This experimental feature currently requires Unix. It retains one supported
library source file; use \fB\-p\fR and \fB\-\-lib\fR to select the library. Other targets and
unsupported edits use fresh checks. See \fIOhm check sessions\fR <https://doc.rust\-lang.org/cargo/reference/unstable.html#ohm\-check\-session>
for the supported source edits, compatibility checks, and lifecycle.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.sp
\fB\-\-source\fR \fISOURCE\fR
.RS 4
Select the source file whose supported edits may reuse compiler state. The path
is relative to the current directory and must be inside the workspace.
.RE
.sp
Other options are the same as \fBcargo\-check\fR(1), except \fB\-\-no\-session\fR,
\fB\-\-unit\-graph\fR, and \fB\-\-compile\-time\-deps\fR cannot be used when starting a session.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
cargo +ohm \-Zohm\-check\-session start \-p my\-library \-\-lib \-\-source src/math.rs
cargo +ohm check \-p my\-library \-\-lib
cargo +ohm stop
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBcargo\fR(1), \fBcargo\-check\fR(1), \fBcargo\-stop\fR(1)
